WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.850
Holderness, on the East Yorkshire coast.

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:07.630
Over the last 1,000 years, it
has retreated about 2 kilometres.

3
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.870
26 villages listed in the
Domesday survey have been lost.

4
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.950
The cliffs are glacial till.

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.650
One year, a stretch can barely move.

6
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.410
The next, it can lose metres.

7
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:24.170
Since 1951, the council has measured
the cliff retreat every year.

8
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.530
So how do you find a cliff's
real rate of retreat?

9
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.290
Measure once, carefully?

10
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.270
Only after big storms?

11
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:36.050
In this mission, you'll link waves, slumping
and longshore drift to the landforms

12
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.290
they create.

13
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:41.190
Then you'll work with the field
data, and judge what it can tell you.

14
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:45.240
Your mission: find the real
rate of retreat of a clay cliff.
